{
  "format": "consent-txt-agents/1",
  "updated": "2026-10-22",
  "notes": [
    "Curated user-agent table read by compiler/compile.py. Edit it by hand rather than importing ai.robots.txt, whose function field is free text.",
    "category: 'train' agents are blocked when train-ai or train-genai lowers to deny, and 'ai-input' agents when ai-input lowers to deny (advisory, since several operators say robots.txt may not apply to them). 'search' agents are listed for reference and never get a blocking group of their own, because a site-wide search deny becomes noindex and a path-level one a 'User-Agent: *' Disallow that every crawler obeys.",
    "respects_robots: what the operator documents. A false value means the operator says robots.txt may not apply (user-triggered fetchers) or the agent is reported to ignore it.",
    "legacy: a token its operator no longer documents but that is still widely listed, kept so older crawlers stay covered.",
    "Mixed-use crawlers (Googlebot, Bingbot, Applebot) are left out because blocking them removes the site from search."
  ],
  "sources": {
